From ad8bbdddad9a294c152dc7786faa1ddfbff4afe1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:16:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/22] k1om-*-linux: new target

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6: the k1om-*-linux* target (and the older
x86_64-k1om-linux* spelling) is x86_64-linux with linuxk1om.h on top:
KNC as the default ISA for both -march and -mtune, 128-bit long double,
the /lib64/ld-linux-k1om.so.2 dynamic linker, "as --march=k1om" and
"ld -m elf_k1om".  TLS, PIE and assembler probes take the x86-64 path.

gcc/configure is regenerated from its sources.  Intel's tree had it
edited by hand: the --64 assembler probe flag for k1om is carried here
in acinclude.m4, and instead of hard-wiring gcc_cv_ld_ro_rw_mix=
read-write the read-only/read-write section mixing probe assembles its
objects with --march=k1om (a bare gas 2.22 emits x86-64 objects, which
the k1om ld rejects, so the probe came out "unknown" and
.gcc_except_table became writable).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
---
 gcc/acinclude.m4            |  4 ++--
 gcc/config.gcc              | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++----------
 gcc/config/i386/linuxk1om.h | 47 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 gcc/configure               | 23 +++++++++++-------
 gcc/configure.ac            | 19 +++++++++------
 5 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 gcc/config/i386/linuxk1om.h

diff --git a/gcc/acinclude.m4 b/gcc/acinclude.m4
index a8962a9b29c..61d436e51f0 100644
--- a/gcc/acinclude.m4
+++ b/gcc/acinclude.m4
@@ -505,7 +505,7 @@ AC_DEFUN([gcc_GAS_FLAGS],
     as_32_opt=-m32
     as_64_opt=-m64
     ;;
-  i?86-*-*:* | x86_64-*-*:* | sparc*-*-*:*)
+  i?86-*-*:* | x86_64-*-*:* | k1om-*-*:* | sparc*-*-*:*)
     dnl Otherwise x86 and SPARC use GNU assembler options --32/--64/--x32.
     case "$target" in
       i?86-*-* | sparc-*-*)
@@ -517,7 +517,7 @@ AC_DEFUN([gcc_GAS_FLAGS],
       x86_64-*-linux-gnuabi32 | x86_64-*-mingw32abi32)
 	gcc_cv_as_flags=--32
 	;;
-      x86_64-*-* | sparcv9-*-* | sparc64-*-*)
+      x86_64-*-* | k1om-*-* | sparcv9-*-* | sparc64-*-*)
 	gcc_cv_as_flags=--64
 	;;
     esac
